WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.920
Series CERN and the Primordial Collision

00:02.920 --> 00:05.280
Season 1, Episode 1

00:05.280 --> 00:06.960
In the aftermath of World War II,

00:06.960 --> 00:11.520
Europe lay devastated, its scientific community scattered and its future uncertain.

00:11.520 --> 00:15.280
Amidst this uncertainty, however, a beacon of hope emerged.

00:15.280 --> 00:19.640
The year was 1954, the dawn of a new epoch in European science.

00:19.640 --> 00:23.480
Twelve nations, each with their own rich history and cultural differences,

00:23.480 --> 00:26.200
came together in unprecedented solidarity.

00:26.200 --> 00:29.200
Their common goal, the pursuit of scientific knowledge.

00:29.280 --> 00:31.560
They sought to rebuild not just their nations,

00:31.560 --> 00:34.840
but the very fabric of scientific understanding.

00:34.840 --> 00:39.000
It wasn't about power, territory or economic gain.

00:39.000 --> 00:44.640
It was about collaboration, discovery and the unquenchable thirst for knowledge.

00:44.640 --> 00:49.640
They knew that by working together, they could achieve far more than they ever could alone.

00:49.640 --> 00:55.080
This was a new kind of diplomacy, one rooted in shared curiosity and mutual respect.

00:55.120 --> 01:00.600
This was a commitment to peace, to progress and to the power of human intellect.

01:00.600 --> 01:05.520
And so, CERN, the European Organisation for Nuclear Research, was born,

01:05.520 --> 01:08.120
promising a new era of scientific discovery.

01:08.120 --> 01:14.120
From its humble beginnings, CERN quickly evolved into a powerhouse of scientific research.

01:14.120 --> 01:19.320
This European Organisation for Nuclear Research, more popularly known as CERN,

01:19.320 --> 01:24.240
has etched its name in the annals of science through its groundbreaking achievements.

01:24.280 --> 01:28.400
Among the jewels in CERN's crown is the development of the World Wide Web.

01:28.400 --> 01:34.160
Yes, the very internet you're using to watch this video owes its existence to the brilliant minds at CERN.

01:34.160 --> 01:37.800
Created in 1989 by British scientist Tim Berners-Lee,

01:37.800 --> 01:41.560
the Web was initially designed to meet the demand for automatic information sharing

01:41.560 --> 01:45.840
between scientists in universities and institutes around the world.

01:45.840 --> 01:50.760
Today, it has morphed into an indispensable tool that connects billions globally,

01:50.800 --> 01:54.960
transforming the way we learn, work and interact.

01:54.960 --> 01:58.360
But CERN's contributions aren't limited to the digital world.

01:58.360 --> 02:02.760
It's also a beacon of illumination in the realm of particle physics.

02:02.760 --> 02:07.880
The discovery of the Higgs-Boson particle in 2012, often referred to as the God particle,

02:07.880 --> 02:10.440
is one of its most notable feats.

02:10.440 --> 02:13.640
The Higgs-Boson, named after physicist Peter Higgs,

02:13.640 --> 02:17.640
is a subatomic particle that gives other particles their mass.

02:17.640 --> 02:21.320
This discovery, made at CERN's Large Hadron Collider,

02:21.320 --> 02:24.800
the world's largest and most powerful particle accelerator,

02:24.800 --> 02:28.200
has revolutionized our understanding of the universe.

02:28.200 --> 02:32.560
It was the missing piece in the standard model of particle physics.

02:32.560 --> 02:37.840
The theory describing three of the four known fundamental forces in the universe.

02:37.840 --> 02:41.520
These achievements are more than just scientific milestones.

02:41.520 --> 02:46.160
They are pivotal moments that have reshaped our world and our place within it.

02:46.160 --> 02:50.600
Through the World Wide Web, CERN has connected us in ways we never thought possible.

02:50.600 --> 02:52.640
And through the discovery of the Higgs-Boson,

02:52.640 --> 02:56.680
it has deepened our understanding of the very fabric of the universe.

02:56.680 --> 03:00.360
These discoveries, among others, have firmly established CERN

03:00.360 --> 03:04.160
as a leading force in the global scientific community.

03:04.160 --> 03:08.920
From unearthing the secrets of the universe to revolutionizing digital communication,

03:08.920 --> 03:12.520
CERN's achievements stand as a testament to human curiosity

03:12.520 --> 03:14.720
and our relentless pursuit of knowledge.

03:14.720 --> 03:18.920
But the impact of CERN extends far beyond the realm of particle physics.

03:18.920 --> 03:23.080
This isn't just about smashing subatomic particles together at near-light speeds.

03:23.080 --> 03:28.800
This is about humanity, about the world coming together to unlock the mysteries of the universe.

03:28.800 --> 03:32.000
CERN has become a beacon of international cooperation.

03:32.000 --> 03:35.720
It's a place where scientists from all over the globe can put aside their nationalities,

03:35.720 --> 03:40.280
their politics, their biases, and work together towards a common goal.

03:40.280 --> 03:45.200
It's a testament to the power of science as a tool for promoting peace and understanding.

03:45.200 --> 03:47.280
But the impact doesn't stop there.

03:47.280 --> 03:51.040
The technologies developed at CERN have found their way into other fields.

03:51.040 --> 03:52.920
In medicine, for instance.

03:52.920 --> 03:58.680
Particle accelerators similar to those used at CERN are now being used in cancer treatment.

03:58.680 --> 04:03.240
Indeed, CERN serves as a shining example of how science can bring nations together

04:03.240 --> 04:05.960
and improve our everyday lives.

04:05.960 --> 04:09.960
The reach of CERN is truly global, and its influence is profound.

04:09.960 --> 04:14.920
Yet despite its past accomplishments, CERN is not resting on its laurels.

04:14.920 --> 04:18.800
The future of CERN holds promise of even more exciting breakthroughs.

04:18.800 --> 04:23.240
Two of the ambitious projects on the horizon include the Large Hadron Collider Upgrade,

04:23.240 --> 04:27.760
known as the High Luminosity LHC, and the Future Circular Collider,

04:27.760 --> 04:33.080
a particle accelerator that dwarfs its predecessors in both size and potential.

04:33.080 --> 04:37.600
The High Luminosity LHC will enhance the collider's capacity to generate data,

04:37.600 --> 04:41.840
revealing insights into the fundamental properties of the universe.

04:41.840 --> 04:47.040
Meanwhile, the Future Circular Collider, with its planned circumference of 100 km,

04:47.040 --> 04:50.720
is set to push the boundaries of our knowledge even further.

04:50.720 --> 04:56.480
This colossal machine aims to answer the deepest questions about the universe's structure and origin.

04:56.480 --> 05:02.240
These future projects embody CERN's commitment to expanding the frontier of human knowledge.

05:02.240 --> 05:05.640
As we stand on the brink of a new era of discovery,

05:05.640 --> 05:08.680
one thing is certain, CERN will continue to lead the way.

